{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 with multiprofile+avgpool is the best RNA-only model (0.6501 acc, config_005). The sole multimodal experiment (config_030: scvi_n200 + resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) scored 0.6315, actually worse than RNA-only, suggesting concat fusion with a weak image encoder (~0.21 alone) introduces noise. Image-only models are very weak (0.21–0.23), so the image signal is marginal. Question: Does weighted fusion allow the model to downweight the noisy image channel and recover (or exceed) RNA-only performance? This is a minimal change from config_030 (only concat→weighted), isolating the fusion mechanism. Why best next experiment: It directly diagnoses whether the multimodal underperformance is a fusion artifact or a fundamental lack of complementary image information. If weighted recovers to ~0.65, the image adds no value but is harmless; if it exceeds 0.65, there is hidden complementary signal; if it stays at ~0.63, the image is actively harmful regardless of fusion. This single result sharply narrows the remaining multimodal search space and is more informative than swapping the image encoder (which is weak either way) or testing transformer aggregation (already shown ≈ avgpool for scvi_n200)."
}

